{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "description": "Chart 16 — Does proximity to transport help venues survive, and for how long? One cohort of venues (every Victorian liquor licence held in July 2022) tracked forward: a 'Survival horizon' dropdown asks whether each venue was still licensed 1, 2 or 3 years later (the July 2023 / 2024 / 2025 snapshots), broken down by walking distance to the nearest stop and split metro (teal) / regional (orange). Survival slides DOWN as the horizon lengthens, but stays flat across the distance bands: being near a stop buys a venue no extra years. Lines/points (not bars) so the y-axis can zoom to the band where the small differences live without a misleading truncated-bar baseline. Survival is a proxy: a ceased licence can be a sale/relocation/rename, not only a closure — association, never causation. Distance is measured against present-day stops, so the older the cohort the more approximate (one stops file). Data: chart_survival_distance_band.csv (8 rows per horizon). NOTE: when new licences_YYYY-07.xlsx snapshots are added and derive_survival.py is rerun, it prints the exact 'horizonYears options' / 'y scale.domain' / 'overall floors by horizon' to keep this hand-maintained spec in sync.",
  "title": {
    "text": "Being near transport doesn't keep venues open",
    "subtitle": [
      "Venues licensed in July 2022, by distance to the nearest stop. Pick how long they had to stay open —",
      "1, 2 or 3 years. Survival slips as the years pass, but stays flat across distance: closeness buys no extra years."
    ],
    "anchor": "start",
    "subtitleFontStyle": "italic"
  },
  "width": "container",
  "height": 340,
  "data": {
    "url": "data/chart_survival_distance_band.csv"
  },
  "params": [
    {
      "name": "horizonYears",
      "value": 2,
      "bind": {
        "input": "select",
        "options": [
          1,
          2,
          3
        ],
        "labels": [
          "1 year (still open July 2023)",
          "2 years (still open July 2024)",
          "3 years (still open July 2025)"
        ],
        "name": "Survival horizon: "
      }
    }
  ],
  "transform": [
    {
      "filter": "datum.horizon_years == horizonYears"
    }
  ],
  "layer": [
    {
      "description": "Survival-floor reference: the venue-weighted share of the whole 2022 cohort still licensed at the chosen horizon, drawn as the baseline every distance band hovers around. Data-driven (overall_survival_pct), so it drops as the horizon lengthens.",
      "transform": [
        {
          "aggregate": [
            {
              "op": "min",
              "field": "overall_survival_pct",
              "as": "floor"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "mark": {
        "type": "rule",
        "strokeDash": [
          4,
          4
        ],
        "strokeWidth": 1,
        "color": "#8c8c8c"
      },
      "encoding": {
        "y": {
          "field": "floor",
          "type": "quantitative",
          "scale": {
            "domain": [
              65,
              92
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "transform": [
        {
          "aggregate": [
            {
              "op": "min",
              "field": "overall_survival_pct",
              "as": "floor"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "calculate": "'≈' + format(datum.floor, '.0f') + '% of the cohort survives — near or far'",
          "as": "label"
        }
      ],
      "mark": {
        "type": "text",
        "align": "left",
        "baseline": "bottom",
        "dy": -3,
        "fontSize": 10,
        "fontStyle": "italic",
        "color": "#8c8c8c"
      },
      "encoding": {
        "x": {
          "value": 5
        },
        "y": {
          "field": "floor",
          "type": "quantitative",
          "scale": {
            "domain": [
              65,
              92
            ]
          }
        },
        "text": {
          "field": "label",
          "type": "nominal"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "mark": {
        "type": "line",
        "strokeWidth": 3,
        "point": {
          "size": 70,
          "filled": true
        }
      },
      "encoding": {
        "x": {
          "field": "distance_band",
          "type": "ordinal",
          "title": "Walking distance to nearest public-transport stop",
          "sort": {
            "field": "distance_band_order"
          },
          "axis": {
            "labelAngle": 0
          }
        },
        "y": {
          "field": "survival_rate_pct",
          "type": "quantitative",
          "title": "Still licensed at the chosen horizon (%)",
          "scale": {
            "domain": [
              65,
              92
            ]
          }
        },
        "color": {
          "field": "metro_regional",
          "type": "nominal",
          "title": "Region",
          "scale": {
            "domain": [
              "Metro",
              "Regional"
            ],
            "range": [
              "#1b9e77",
              "#d95f02"
            ]
          }
        },
        "tooltip": [
          {
            "field": "metro_regional",
            "type": "nominal",
            "title": "Region"
          },
          {
            "field": "distance_band",
            "type": "ordinal",
            "title": "Distance band"
          },
          {
            "field": "horizon_label",
            "type": "nominal",
            "title": "Survival horizon"
          },
          {
            "field": "survival_rate_pct",
            "type": "quantitative",
            "title": "Still licensed",
            "format": ".1f"
          },
          {
            "field": "survived_count",
            "type": "quantitative",
            "title": "Venues surviving",
            "format": ","
          },
          {
            "field": "cohort_count",
            "type": "quantitative",
            "title": "Venues in band (2022)",
            "format": ","
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "mark": {
        "type": "text",
        "dy": -12,
        "fontWeight": "bold",
        "fontSize": 11
      },
      "encoding": {
        "x": {
          "field": "distance_band",
          "type": "ordinal",
          "sort": {
            "field": "distance_band_order"
          }
        },
        "y": {
          "field": "survival_rate_pct",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "color": {
          "field": "metro_regional",
          "type": "nominal",
          "scale": {
            "domain": [
              "Metro",
              "Regional"
            ],
            "range": [
              "#1b9e77",
              "#d95f02"
            ]
          },
          "legend": null
        },
        "text": {
          "field": "survival_rate_pct",
          "type": "quantitative",
          "format": ".0f"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "values": [
          {}
        ]
      },
      "mark": {
        "type": "text",
        "align": "right",
        "baseline": "top",
        "fontStyle": "italic",
        "fontSize": 12,
        "color": "#666",
        "x": {
          "expr": "width"
        },
        "y": 4,
        "text": {
          "expr": "'July 2022 cohort, ' + horizonYears + (horizonYears == 1 ? ' year on' : ' years on')"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Caveat badge reminding the reader that survival is a licence-presence proxy, not a direct closure measure.",
      "data": {
        "values": [
          {}
        ]
      },
      "mark": {
        "type": "text",
        "align": "left",
        "baseline": "top",
        "fontStyle": "italic",
        "fontSize": 10,
        "color": "#999",
        "x": {
          "expr": "4"
        },
        "y": {
          "expr": "4"
        },
        "text": "survival = licence presence (proxy)"
      }
    }
  ]
}
